//   unmodified character that would be generated by pressing the key, or an `SDLK_*` constant for
//   those keys that do not generate characters. A special exception is the number keys at the top
//   of the keyboard which map by default to SDLK_0...SDLK_9 on AZERTY layouts. Keys with the
//   `SDLK_EXTENDED_MASK` bit set do not map to a scancode or Unicode code point. Many common
//   keycodes are listed below, but this list is not exhaustive.
